  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145740",
      "title": "\"getServerSideProps\" and its Context",
      "lectureOrder": 283,
      "videoOrder": 264,
      "sourceHash": "435267fde9f96953286757eeabfcaaa139402d086819ad9b464bc05ef5c49397",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 5.46,
          "en": "So, which implications does getServerSideProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.46,
          "end": 9.09,
          "en": "running on the server only have for us?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.09,
          "end": 13.15,
          "en": "The implications can be found in this context object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.15,
          "end": 16.73,
          "en": "unlike context in getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.73,
          "end": 19.4,
          "en": "we don't just have access to the params",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.4,
          "end": 22.95,
          "en": "and a couple of other less important fields",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.95,
          "end": 27.48,
          "en": "instead, we get access to the full request object as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.48,
          "end": 30.31,
          "en": "And also to the response which will be sent back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.31,
          "end": 32.67,
          "en": "so that we could even manipulate this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.67,
          "end": 36.27,
          "en": "and add extra headers if you wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.27,
          "end": 40.29,
          "en": "To be precise we do get a couple of values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.29,
          "end": 42.88,
          "en": "a couple of keys in this context object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.88,
          "end": 46.01,
          "en": "and we do get access still to the params",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.01,
          "end": 49.94,
          "en": "that does not change if we have this on a dynamic page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.94,
          "end": 51.24,
          "en": "which we don't have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.24,
          "end": 53.58,
          "en": "but if this would be on a dynamic page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.58,
          "end": 56.35,
          "en": "we still would get access to params",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.35,
          "end": 59.88,
          "en": "but in addition, as mentioned, we also get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.88,
          "end": 62.823,
          "en": "to the request object and the response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.67,
          "end": 66.37,
          "en": "Now, if you know a bit of Node.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.37,
          "end": 68.83,
          "en": "and especially of Express.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.83,
          "end": 70.71000000000001,
          "en": "this might look familiar to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.71000000000001,
          "end": 73.17,
          "en": "There you also can write server side code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.17,
          "end": 76.45,
          "en": "where you get a request object and the response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.45,
          "end": 78.72,
          "en": "and you can then manipulate the response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.72,
          "end": 81.813,
          "en": "as needed to send back an appropriate response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.8,
          "end": 83.88,
          "en": "Now, you don't need to worry",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.88,
          "end": 85.96000000000001,
          "en": "about sending back a response here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.96000000000001,
          "end": 88.05,
          "en": "Next.js will do that for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.05,
          "end": 90.12,
          "en": "it will be derendered component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.12,
          "end": 92.17,
          "en": "but you can manipulate the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.17,
          "end": 96.28,
          "en": "before it's sent back by adding extra headers, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.28,
          "end": 99.05,
          "en": "by adding a cookie, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.05,
          "end": 102.15,
          "en": "In addition, you can also dive into the request object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.15,
          "end": 104.25,
          "en": "that reached the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.25,
          "end": 107.24000000000001,
          "en": "and you can read incoming data from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.24000000000001,
          "end": 110.4,
          "en": "For example, headers that were attached through request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.4,
          "end": 114.28,
          "en": "and therefore cookie data that was attached to the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.28,
          "end": 116.83,
          "en": "Request and response the objects we're getting here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.83,
          "end": 121.49,
          "en": "are your official Node.js default incoming message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.49,
          "end": 123.87,
          "en": "and response objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.87,
          "end": 127.62,
          "en": "So, here I will briefly lock the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.62,
          "end": 130.6,
          "en": "and then also lock the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.6,
          "end": 134.38,
          "en": "so that we can get a closer look at them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.38,
          "end": 139.38,
          "en": "If I save this and I reload user profile",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.76,
          "end": 144.04,
          "en": "now this code executed again and now we see a long log here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.04,
          "end": 146.41,
          "en": "because these are quite complex objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.41,
          "end": 150.4,
          "en": "with a lot of built in methods and properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.4,
          "end": 152.07,
          "en": "So, you'll see there's a lot in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.07,
          "end": 155.36,
          "en": "and you definitely don't need to go through all of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.36,
          "end": 158.82,
          "en": "But for example, you see that there are headers in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.82,
          "end": 161.183,
          "en": "which we could extract if we wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.68,
          "end": 163.95,
          "en": "Now, we don't need this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.95,
          "end": 166.09,
          "en": "but it will become more important later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.09,
          "end": 168.35,
          "en": "once we talk about authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.35,
          "end": 170.93,
          "en": "Now, I will quit this here and not go through all of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.93,
          "end": 173.88,
          "en": "but you can definitely take a close look at that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.88,
          "end": 177.88,
          "en": "And these again are the default node objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.88,
          "end": 180.88,
          "en": "for incoming messages and for responses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.88,
          "end": 183.76,
          "en": "And I'll link the documentation of these objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.76,
          "end": 186.88,
          "en": "to this lecture so that you can take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.88,
          "end": 190.51,
          "en": "at what's in them in the official docs as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.51,
          "end": 192.7,
          "en": "And getting access to this kind of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.7,
          "end": 195.74,
          "en": "can sometimes be important if you, again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.74,
          "end": 199.56,
          "en": "for example, needs special header or cookie data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.56,
          "end": 201.5,
          "en": "And now another reason as mentioned before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.5,
          "end": 204.01,
          "en": "for using getServerSideProps could be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 204.01,
          "end": 207.81,
          "en": "that you don't need request or response specific data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.81,
          "end": 211.23,
          "en": "that you don't need to work with request or response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.23,
          "end": 214.43,
          "en": "but that you really wanna ensure that this function runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.43,
          "end": 216.82,
          "en": "for every incoming request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216.82,
          "end": 219.89,
          "en": "so that it's never static pre-generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.89,
          "end": 223.46,
          "en": "Because for example you have highly dynamic data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.46,
          "end": 226.01,
          "en": "which changes multiple times every second",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 226.01,
          "end": 228.84,
          "en": "and therefore, you know, that any old page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 228.84,
          "end": 232.45,
          "en": "you would be serving would already be outdated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 232.45,
          "end": 235.86,
          "en": "That could be another reason for using getServiceSideProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.87,
          "end": 238.96,
          "en": "but as you see using it is simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 238.96,
          "end": 241.72,
          "en": "You can still write any server side code in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 241.72,
          "end": 245.27,
          "en": "You can still reach out to the dummy-backend.json file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.27,
          "end": 247.4,
          "en": "as we did it before, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 247.4,
          "end": 249.04,
          "en": "and you still return the props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.04,
          "end": 251.26,
          "en": "for the component function at the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.26,
          "end": 253.6,
          "en": "The only key difference is the kind of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 253.6,
          "end": 255.81,
          "en": "you get access to in the context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 255.81,
          "end": 258.673,
          "en": "and the timing of this function.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
